<div dir=3D"auto">&gt; Yes, Meta has a good article on the topic</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">&gt; <a href=3D"https://engineering.fb.com/2024/05/22/sec=
urity/post-quantum-readiness-tls-pqr-meta/" target=3D"_blank">
https://engineering.fb.com/2024/05/22/security/post-quantum-readiness-tls-p=
qr-meta/</a></div>
<div dir=3D"ltr"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">This is a good article=E2=80=94 I want to highlight that =
Meta deployed Kyber/ML-KEM-512 only on their internal connections, and don&=
#39;t seem to have any plans to roll that out to their external connections=
. While -512 nicely fits existing infra, and I
 agree it should be available especially for IoT settings and internal depl=
oyments like Meta&#39;s, in general public internet settings it seems to be=
 a a little riskier as a right-on-the-line parameter set for NIST Level 1 s=
ecurity than say -768, which has more
 headroom security-wise.=C2=A0</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr"><br>
</div>
